KJV: Shuah.

H7745.definition:
from H7743 (שׁוּחַ);
a chasm
KJV: ditch, pit.

H7746.definition:
the same as H7745 (שׁוּחָה);
Shuchah, an Israelite
KJV: Shuah.

H7747.definition:
patronymic from H7744 (שׁוּחַ);
a Shuchite or descendant of Shuach
KJV: Shuhite.

H7748.definition:
from H7743 (שׁוּחַ); humbly;
Shucham, an Israelite
KJV: Shuham.

H7749.definition:
patronymic from H7748 (שׁוּחָם);
a Shuchamite (collectively)
KJV: Shuhamites.

H7750.definition:
or (by permutation) סוּט; a primitive root;
to detrude, i.e. (intransitively and figuratively) become derelict (wrongly practise; namely, idolatry)
KJV: turn aside to.

H7751.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to push forth; (but used only figuratively) to lash, i.e. (the sea with oars) to row; by implication, to travel
KJV: go (about, through, to and fro), mariner, rower, run to and fro.

H7752.definition:
from H7751 (שׁוּט);
a lash (literally or figuratively)
KJV: scourge, whip.

H7753.definition:
a primitive root;
to entwine, i.e. shut in (for formation, protection or restraint)
KJV: fence, (make an) hedge (up).

H7754.definition:
or (feminine) שׂוֹכָה; from H7753 (שׂוּךְ);
a branch (as interleaved)
KJV: bough.

H7755.definition:
or שֹׂכֹה; or שׂוֹכוֹ; from H7753 (שׂוּךְ);
Sokoh or Soko, the name of two places in Palestine
KJV: Shocho, Shochoh, Sochoh, Soco, Socoh.

H7756.definition:
probably patronymic from a name corresponding to H7754 (שׂוֹךְ) (feminine);
a Sukathite or descendant of an unknown Israelite named Sukah
KJV: Suchathite.

H7757.definition:
from an unused root meaning to hang down;
a skirt; by implication, a bottom edge
KJV: hem, skirt, train.

H7758.definition:
or שֵׁילָל; (Micah 1:8), from H7997 (שָׁלַל);
nude (especially bare-foot); by implication, captive
KJV: spoiled, stripped.

H7759.definition:
from H7999 (שָׁלַם);
peaceful (with the article always prefixed, making it a pet name); the Shulammith, an epithet of Solomon's queen
KJV: Shulamite.

H7760.definition:
or שִׂים; a primitive root;
to put (used in a great variety of applications, literal, figurative, inferentially, and elliptically)
KJV: [idiom] any wise, appoint, bring, call (a name), care, cast in, change, charge, commit, consider, convey, determine, [phrase] disguise, dispose, do, get, give, heap up, hold, impute, lay (down, up), leave, look, make (out), mark, [phrase] name, [idiom] on, ordain, order, [phrase] paint, place, preserve, purpose, put (on), [phrase] regard, rehearse, reward, (cause to) set (on, up), shew, [phrase] stedfastly, take, [idiom] tell, [phrase] tread down, (over-)turn, [idiom] wholly, work.

H7761.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H7760 (שׂוּם)
{to put (used in a great variety of applications, literal, figurative, inferentially, and elliptically)}
KJV: [phrase] command, give, lay, make, [phrase] name, [phrase] regard, set.

H7762.definition:
from an unused root meaning to exhale;
garlic (from its rank odor)
KJV: garlic.

H7763.definition:
or שֹׁמֵר; active participle of H8104 (שָׁמַר); keeper;
