KJV: Shomer.

H7764.definition:
from an unused root meaning to rest; quiet;
Shuni, an Israelite
KJV: Shuni.

H7765.definition:
patronymic from H7764 (שׁוּנִי);
a Shunite (collectively) or descendants of Shuni
KJV: Shunites.

H7766.definition:
probably from the same as H7764 (שׁוּנִי); quietly;
Shunem, a place in Pal
KJV: Shunem.

H7767.definition:
patrial from H7766 (שׁוּנֵם);
a Shunammitess, or female inhabitant of Shunem
KJV: Shunamite.

H7768.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to be free; but used only causatively and reflexively, to halloo (for help, i.e. freedom from some trouble)
KJV: cry (aloud, out), shout.

H7769.definition:
from H7768 (שָׁוַע);
a halloo
KJV: cry, riches.

H7770.definition:
the same as H7769 (שׁוּעַ);
Shua, a Canaanite
KJV: Shua, Shuah.

H7771.definition:
from H7768 (שָׁוַע) in the original sense of freedom;
a noble, i.e. liberal, opulent; also (as noun in the derived sense) a halloo
KJV: bountiful, crying, rich.

H7772.definition:
the same as H7771 (שׁוֹעַ); rich;
Shoa, an Oriental people
KJV: Shoa.

H7773.definition:
from H7768 (שָׁוַע);
a halloo
KJV: cry.

H7774.definition:
from H7768 (שָׁוַע); wealth;
Shua, an Israelitess
KJV: Shua.

H7775.definition:
feminine of H7773 (שֶׁוַע);
a hallooing
KJV: crying.

H7776.definition:
or שֻׁעָל; from the same as H8168 (שֹׁעַל);
a jackal (as a burrower)
KJV: fox.

H7777.definition:
the same as H7776 (שׁוּעָל);
Shual, the name of an Israelite and of a place in Palestine
KJV: Shual.

H7778.definition:
or שֹׁעֵר active participle of H8176 (שָׁעַר) (as denominative from H8179 (שַׁעַר));
a janitor
KJV: doorkeeper, porter.

H7779.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to gape, i.e. snap at; figuratively, to overwhelm
KJV: break, bruise, cover.

H7780.definition:
from H8210 (שָׁפַךְ); poured;
Shophak, a Syrian
KJV: Shophach.

H7781.definition:
patronymic from H8197 (שְׁפוּפָם);
a Shuphamite (collectively) or descendants of Shephupham
KJV: Shuphamite.

H7782.definition:
or שֹׁפָר; from H8231 (שָׁפַר) in the original sense of incising;
a cornet (as giving a clear sound) or curved horn
KJV: cornet, trumpet.

H7783.definition:
a primitive root;
to run after or over, i.e. overflow
KJV: overflow, water.

H7784.definition:
from H7783 (שׁוּק);
a street (as run over)
KJV: street.

H7785.definition:
from H7783 (שׁוּק);
the (lower) leg (as a runner)
KJV: hip, leg, shoulder, thigh.

H7786.definition:
